  <h1>Looped World Models: Depth That Scales with Complexity</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    World models need deep computation for hard transitions but waste it on easy ones.
    LoopWM is the first looped transformer architecture for world modelling — one parameter-shared block
    applied iteratively, exiting early for free-flight steps and running deep for complex events.
    A 1B-parameter LoopWM outperforms Claude Opus 4.6 Max on ScienceWorld by +21 pp, using 100× fewer parameters.
  </p>
