<h3>AlfWorld — Overall</h3>
<p>
  On AlfWorld (household tasks), LoopWM is competitive: 51.6% EM vs Claude's 53.0% EM,
  with LoopWM winning on BLEU-4 (71.6% vs 66.8%) and Token F1 (80.4% vs 72.6%). The
  1B specialized model essentially matches a frontier LLM at a fraction of the resource cost.
</p>
<div class="callout">
  <strong>New scaling axis:</strong> LoopWM establishes <em>iterative latent depth</em> as a new
  dimension for world model scaling — orthogonal to model size and data volume. More loop iterations
  at inference time yields progressively refined predictions, analogous to test-time compute scaling
  in language models (Geiping et al., 2025).
</div>

<!-- Listen-friendly content -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display:none" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: Looped World Models</h2>
    <p>World models predict how environments evolve, but today's fixed-depth architectures apply the same computation to every transition, whether simple or complex. This wastes compute on easy steps and under-serves hard ones. Looped World Models, or LoopWM, resolve this by replacing a stack of unique layers with one parameter-shared transformer block applied iteratively. The same weights are reused at every iteration, decoupling effective depth from parameter count — up to 100 times more parameter-efficient than conventional approaches.</p>
    <p>A lightweight exit gate checks the hidden state after each iteration and terminates early when the transition has converged, allocating just 1-2 loops to simple navigation and 6-8 loops to complex chemical reactions or contact events. A spectral norm constraint on the state-retention matrix ensures all eigenvalues remain in (0,1), giving provably stable rollouts across hundreds of steps. Deferred decoding further reduces compute by running all K latent transitions silently and decoding only once at the final step. On ScienceWorld, a 1-billion-parameter LoopWM beats Claude Opus 4.6 Max by 21 percentage points on exact match, using over 100 times fewer parameters. On AlfWorld it is essentially competitive with the frontier model.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：循环世界模型</h2>
    <p>世界模型的核心任务是预测环境状态的演变，但现有的固定深度架构对每一步转换施加同等的计算量，无论转换是简单还是复杂。这在容易的步骤上浪费了算力，在困难的步骤上又力不从心。循环世界模型LoopWM通过将多个独立层替换为一个参数共享的Transformer模块并反复迭代来解决这一矛盾，在参数数量不变的情况下实现高达100倍的参数效率提升。</p>
    <p>一个轻量的退出门控在每次迭代后检查隐藏状态，当转换收敛时提前终止循环——简单导航只需1到2次迭代，复杂化学反应或碰撞事件则运行6到8次。状态保留矩阵上的谱范数约束确保所有特征值维持在0到1之间，从数学上保证了数百步推演中的稳定性。延迟解码进一步降低计算量：沿K步动作序列在隐空间中静默推演，仅在最终步骤解码一次。在ScienceWorld基准上，仅10亿参数的LoopWM在精确匹配率上以21个百分点的优势超越Claude Opus 4.6 Max，参数量不及后者的百分之一。在AlfWorld上则与前沿模型旗鼓相当。</p>
  </div>
